{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966816,"nonce":"sL7fEUSM3sjsKn0FoMANyJO95AQ=","title":"WebGL2 fallback status","message":"WebGL2 fallback (data texture + vertex buffer) for devices where browser WebGPU isn't available (e.g., Pixel 10 Pro PowerVR GPU not on Chrome's WebGPU allowlist).\n\n**Working on WebGL2 (all verified on Pixel 10 Pro Chrome):**\n- SDF pipelines (core, shadow, 3D, notch) — via `sdf_*_dt.wgsl` shaders\n- Text pipeline — via `text_dt.wgsl`\n- Glass pipelines — via `glass_dt.wgsl`, `simple_glass_dt.wgsl`\n- Mesh pipeline — via `mesh_dt.wgsl` (joint matrices as texture)\n- Surface format: `Rgba8Unorm` (non-sRGB to avoid double gamma)\n- Vertex buffer fallback for vertex shader data\n- canvas_demo and mesh_3d_demo both render correctly\n\n**Known rendering issues on WebGL2:**\n- Distance fade card in pointer_query_demo cuts/corrupts the page when scrolled into view — likely related to layer effects needing COPY_SRC (dropped on GL adapter surface) for two-pass compositing\n- Glass morphism skipped (no per-frame glass data texture plumbing)\n\n**Limited on WebGL2:**\n- Glass morphism — skipped (DT shaders exist: `glass_dt.wgsl`, `simple_glass_dt.wgsl`; needs per-frame glass data texture + bind group plumbing in renderer)\n- Particles — skipped (requires compute shaders for simulation, which WebGL2 lacks). `particle_render_dt.wgsl` exists for future compute-free particle path\n\n**Why:** `navigator.gpu.requestAdapter()` returns null on Pixel 10 Pro despite `chrome://gpu` showing \"WebGPU: Hardware accelerated\". Chrome's internal device allowlist doesn't include PowerVR/Tensor G5 for web content WebGPU.\n\n**How to apply:** Mesh/Glass/Particles each need their own DT shader variants + conditional bind group layouts, following the SDF pattern.","files":null}]}